.\" zvolcarve(1) — manual page, mdoc. Kept true to the program by
.\" tests/man-check.sh.
.Dd September 26, 2026
.Dt ZVOLCARVE 1
.Os zvolrescue 0.9.7
.Sh NAME
.Nm zvolcarve
.Nd find and extract volumes that no uberblock of a ZFS pool points at any more
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar global options
.Cm scan
.Fl o Ar dir
.Op Ar options
.Op Ar dev ...
.Nm
.Op Ar global options
.Cm list
.Ar dir
.Nm
.Op Ar global options
.Cm dump
.Ar dir candidate
.Op Ar dev ...
.Fl o Ar out.img
.Op Ar options
.Nm
.Op Ar global options
.Cm roots
.Fl o Ar dir
.Op Ar options
.Op Ar dev ...
.Nm
.Op Ar global options
.Cm zeropoint
.Op Ar options
.Op Ar dev ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
When the transaction groups that named a volume have been overwritten,
its blocks may still be on the members, addressed by nothing.
.Nm
scans the raw space of the members for the metadata of such volumes,
ranks what it finds into candidates in a workspace directory, and
extracts a candidate block by block, every block verified by its own
checksum.
.Cm roots
does the same for the pool's object set when no uberblock survives,
and
.Cm zeropoint
finds where a member's vdev begins from the pointers alone.
Nothing is written to the members.
.Pp
The global options and the pool member options are those of
.Xr zvolrescue 1 :
.Fl f , Fl -format Ar text | json ,
.Fl v , Fl -verbose ,
.Fl q , Fl -quiet ,
.Fl -evidence-log ,
.Fl -hash-inputs ,
.Fl -no-color ,
.Fl -debug ,
.Fl -debug-log ,
and
.Fl -image ,
.Fl -hints ,
.Fl -search-order ,
.Fl -pool-guid ,
.Fl -assume-member ,
.Fl -ignore-unknown-features ,
.Fl -map ,
.Fl -device-may-fail ,
.Fl -surface-scan-on-device .
.Sh COMMANDS
.Ss scan
.Nm Cm scan
.Fl o Ar dir
.Op Ar options
.Op Ar dev ...
.Pp
Scan the members and record what could be a volume.
A profile of the volume being looked for narrows the search; without
one every recognised dnode is a candidate.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl o , Fl -output Ar dir
The carve workspace, where candidates and the scan's state go.
.It Fl -volblocksize Ar bytes
Data block size of the volume being looked for.
.It Fl -levels Ar n
Tree depth of the volume being looked for.
.It Fl -txg Ar from Ns .. Ns Ar to
Birth transaction group window.
.It Fl -size Ar min Ns .. Ns Ar max
Estimated size range in bytes.
.It Fl -dnode-type Ar type
Object type to look for:
.Ql zvol
(the default),
.Ql file ,
a numeric dnode type, or
.Ql any .
.It Fl -profile Ar file
Read the profile from a JSON file; command-line fields win.
.It Fl -like Ar dataset
Take the block size, levels and size from a dataset that still exists
in the pool: in most incidents the lost volume was made like its
neighbours.
.It Fl -strict-profile
Treat profile fields as hard filters, not as hints.
.It Fl -range Ar start Ns - Ns Ar end
Only this byte range of each member.
.It Fl -resume
Continue a scan that was interrupted; a SIGINT or SIGTERM ends a scan
with its state written (exit status 6).
.It Fl -full-assess
Read every block a candidate claims when ranking it, rather than a
sample.
Slow, and rarely worth it before a
.Cm dump .
.It Fl -max-hits Ar n
Stop after this many candidates; default 100000.
.It Fl -sample Ar n
Report what the first
.Ar n
hits look like instead of filtering, so a profile can be picked from
the disk.
.It Fl -compressed Ar list
Compressions to try at each allocation-aligned offset:
.Ql lz4,lzjb,gzip,zstd
(the default), a subset, or
.Ql none
for the plaintext pass alone.
Metadata is lz4 on any modern pool and lzjb on one made before the
.Ql lz4_compress
feature; each one costs a pass, and dropping the wrong one finds
nothing.
.El
.Ss list
.Nm Cm list
.Ar dir
.Pp
Show the candidates a previous scan found, ranked, with the id each
one is extracted by.
.Ss dump
.Nm Cm dump
.Ar dir candidate
.Op Ar dev ...
.Fl o Ar out.img
.Op Ar options
.Pp
Extract one candidate, verifying every block by its checksum.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl o , Fl -output Ar out.img
Write the image here.
.It Fl -strict
Stop at the first block that cannot be read.
.It Fl -size Ar bytes
Extract this many bytes instead of what the dnode implies.
.It Fl -hash Ar list
Also hash the image with
.Ql md5
and/or
.Ql sha1 ,
comma-separated; SHA-256 is always taken.
.It Fl -resume
Continue an interrupted extraction of the same candidate; the state is
kept in
.Pa out.img.resume.json
while a run is in progress.
.El
.Ss roots
.Nm Cm roots
.Fl o Ar dir
.Op Ar options
.Op Ar dev ...
.Pp
Find the pool's object set when no uberblock survives: the members are
scanned for object set headers, which are ranked into
.Ar dir .
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl o , Fl -output Ar dir
Carve workspace, where the ranked headers are written.
.It Fl -range Ar start Ns - Ns Ar end
Only this byte range of each member.
.It Fl -compressed Ar list
Compressions to try, as in
.Cm scan .
.It Fl -max-roots Ar n
Keep at most this many headers after ranking; default 32.
.El
.Ss zeropoint
.Nm Cm zeropoint
.Op Ar options
.Op Ar dev ...
.Pp
Where the vdev begins, from the pointers alone: the base at which the
block pointers found on a member agree with the checksums of what they
point at.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl o , Fl -output Ar dir
Also write
.Pa zeropoint.json
here.
.It Fl -window Ar start Ns - Ns Ar end
Consider only bases in this byte range; default the first 64 MiB,
where a partition begins.
.It Fl -compressed Ar list
Compressions to try, as in
.Cm scan .
.It Fl -max-hits Ar n
Collect probes from at most this many dnodes; default 4096.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa dir/state.json
The state of a scan, for
.Fl -resume .
.It Pa out.img.resume.json
The state of an interrupted
.Cm dump .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
As in
.Xr zvolrescue 1 :
0 success, 1 usage, 2 evidence unreadable, 3 nothing found or the
candidate unreadable, 4 a partial image, 5 refused, 6 interrupted with
the state written, 7 the medium refused a read.
.Sh EXAMPLES
A volume made like its surviving neighbour, found and extracted from
images of two mirror members:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
zvolcarve scan --like pool/vm/disk1 -o carve \e
    --image ada0.img --image ada1.img
zvolcarve list carve
zvolcarve dump carve 3 --image ada0.img --image ada1.img -o disk0.img
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr zvolfiles 1 ,
.Xr zvolreport 1 ,
.Xr zvolrescue 1 ,
.Xr zvoltimeline 1
